---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base>
  <!-- ═══ Nav ═══ -->
  <nav class="nav">
    <div class="nav__inner">
      <a class="nav__brand" href="#">
        <div class="nav__logo">NS</div>
        <span class="nav__name">Nan Shang</span>
      </a>
      <div class="nav__links">
        <a class="nav__link" href="#overview">Overview</a>
        <a class="nav__link" href="#approach">Approach</a>
        <a class="nav__link" href="#systems">Systems</a>
        <a class="nav__link" href="#work">Work</a>
        <a class="nav__link" href="#research">Research</a>
        <a class="nav__link" href="#contact">Contact</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </nav>

  <!-- ═══ Hero with Aurora ═══ -->
  <div class="hero-wrap dotgrid">
    <div class="wrap">
      <header class="hero">
        <div class="hero__kicker">
          <span class="hero__kicker-dot"></span>
          Chief Scientist & Founding Engineer
        </div>

        <h1 class="hero__h1">I build systems that last.</h1>

        <p class="hero__desc">
          Where data meets uncertainty, and where the real test is not
          performance in isolation — but behavior over time.
        </p>

        <div class="hero__meta">
          <span class="hero__meta-name">Nan Shang, Ph.D.</span>
          <span class="hero__meta-role">Chief Scientist & Founding Engineer</span>
          <span class="hero__meta-org">Drone Institute</span>
        </div>

        <div class="hero__cta">
          <a class="btn btn--primary" href="#overview">Read more</a>
          <a class="btn" href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=TcDAyj0AAAAJ&hl=en"
             target="_blank" rel="noopener">Scholar</a>
          <a class="btn" href="https://github.com/leibowivz"
             target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
          <a class="btn" href="mailto:nan.shang@droneinstitute.ai">Contact</a>
        </div>
      </header>
    </div>

    <!-- Aurora light ribbons -->
    <div class="aurora" aria-hidden="true">
      <div class="aurora__ribbon aurora__r1"></div>
      <div class="aurora__ribbon aurora__r2"></div>
      <div class="aurora__ribbon aurora__r3"></div>
      <div class="aurora__line aurora__l1"></div>
      <div class="aurora__line aurora__l2"></div>
      <div class="aurora__line aurora__l3"></div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <main class="wrap">

    <!-- ═══ Overview ═══ -->
    <section id="overview">
      <div class="sh"><div class="sh__bar"></div><span class="sh__text">Overview</span></div>

      <p class="pull">
        I design and operate production-grade geospatial and AI systems.
      </p>
      <p>
        My work sits at the intersection of remote sensing research, geospatial
        analytics, and system architecture. I build systems that take spatial
        data — often noisy, incomplete, and operationally constrained — and turn
        it into outputs that can be trusted in real decision-making contexts.
      </p>
      <p style="margin-top: 1.25rem;">
        What matters is not isolated model performance, but how a system behaves
        end to end: how data enters, how assumptions propagate, how errors surface,
        and how the system evolves under continuous use.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══ Role ═══ -->
    <section>
      <div class="sh"><div class="sh__bar"></div><span class="sh__text">My Role</span></div>

      <p style="margin-bottom: 1.5rem;">
        As a founding engineer, I designed the core architectures from first
        principles. As chief scientist, I ensure that deployed systems remain
        scientifically grounded as they scale and face real operational pressure.
      </p>
      <ul class="fl">
        <li>Define system-level evaluation criteria beyond accuracy alone</li>
        <li>Architect end-to-end geospatial and AI pipelines</li>
        <li>Translate research methods into deployable, auditable systems</li>
        <li>Own trade-offs across accuracy, latency, cost, and reliability</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══ Approach ═══ -->
    <section id="approach">
      <div class="sh"><div class="sh__bar"></div><span class="sh__text">How I Build Systems</span></div>

      <div class="g2">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__num">01</div>
          <div class="card__title">Production is the benchmark</div>
          <p class="card__body">
            A system is only meaningful if it continues to behave correctly after
            deployment. I design systems to fail visibly, support iteration without
            destabilization, and remain interpretable to operators.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__num">02</div>
          <div class="card__title">Constraints shape architecture</div>
          <p class="card__body">
            Latency, throughput, cost envelopes, and operational friction are
            architectural facts. I make trade-offs explicit so systems can be
            reasoned about and maintained over time.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__num">03</div>
          <div class="card__title">Deployment reveals assumptions</div>
          <p class="card__body">
            Research does not end at deployment. I design feedback loops that
            surface failure modes, quantify drift, and allow systems to improve
            without eroding trust or stability.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__num">04</div>
          <div class="card__title">Data quality compounds</div>
          <p class="card__body">
            Long-term advantage comes from disciplined data practices. I build
            pipelines where ingestion, annotation, quality control, monitoring,
            retraining, and rollback reinforce one another.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══ Systems ═══ -->
    <section id="systems">
      <div class="sh"><div class="sh__bar"></div><span class="sh__text">Systems I Build</span></div>

      <div class="g2">
        <div class="sys sys--pipe">
          <div class="sys__status"><span class="sys__dot"></span>Pipeline</div>
          <div class="sys__title">End-to-End Geospatial</div>
          <p class="sys__body">
            Full lifecycle — ingestion, normalization, processing, verification,
            reporting, delivery. Repeatable, auditable, resilient under scale.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="sys sys--sense">
          <div class="sys__status"><span class="sys__dot"></span>Sensing</div>
          <div class="sys__title">Multimodal Remote Sensing</div>
          <p class="sys__body">
            RGB imagery, thermal and infrared data, derived spatial layers.
            Extracting actionable signals while controlling uncertainty.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="sys sys--qc">
          <div class="sys__status"><span class="sys__dot"></span>Quality</div>
          <div class="sys__title">Verification & QC</div>
          <p class="sys__body">
            Automated and human-in-the-loop layers that surface projection
            errors, alignment drift, and metadata assumptions.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="sys sys--ship">
          <div class="sys__status"><span class="sys__dot"></span>Delivery</div>
          <div class="sys__title">Secure Data Delivery</div>
          <p class="sys__body">
            Multi-tenant access control, lifecycle management, permission
            boundaries, and audit-friendly access patterns.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <!-- ═══ Spectral Strip ═══ -->
  <div class="strip">
    <div class="wrap">
      <div class="strip__inner">
        <div class="strip__band"></div>
        <div class="strip__label">Research Background</div>
        <div class="strip__title">Remote Sensing &<br/>Geospatial Information</div>
        <p class="strip__body">
          My research directly informs the systems I build. These insights shape
          practical decisions — data preprocessing, model selection, validation
          strategies, and quality control thresholds.
        </p>
        <ul class="tags">
          <li>GIS & Spatial Analytics</li>
          <li>LiDAR & Point Clouds</li>
          <li>Remote Sensing</li>
          <li>Geospatial AI</li>
          <li>Production ML</li>
          <li>Earth Observation</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <main class="wrap">

    <!-- ═══ Selected Work ═══ -->
    <section id="work">
      <div class="sh"><div class="sh__bar"></div><span class="sh__text">Selected Work</span></div>

      <p class="aside">
        Public descriptions focus on architectural patterns and operational
        behavior, not on clients, locations, or proprietary metrics.
      </p>

      <div class="g1">
        <div class="card">
          <h3>Production Geospatial Intelligence Platforms</h3>
          <p class="card__body" style="margin-bottom: 1rem;">
            Large-scale platforms built to support continuous operation, repeatable
            results, and controlled iteration under real-world constraints.
          </p>
          <ul class="fl">
            <li>Ingest high-volume spatial data from heterogeneous sources</li>
            <li>Normalize and align across coordinate systems and resolutions</li>
            <li>Execute analytics and inference at scale</li>
            <li>Verification and QC embedded in the execution path</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Multisensor Analysis & Decision Pipelines</h3>
          <p class="card__body">
            Combining RGB imagery, thermal and infrared signals, and derived
            spatial features. Emphasis on extracting decision-relevant signals
            and minimizing false positives where ground truth is incomplete.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <h3>Verification-Centric System Design</h3>
          <ul class="fl">
            <li>Surface spatial inconsistencies — alignment, scale, unit errors</li>
            <li>Detect silent failure modes before downstream impact</li>
            <li>Automated checks integrated with human-in-the-loop review</li>
            <li>Verification artifacts treated as first-class outputs</li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="g2">
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Data-Centric AI Loops</h3>
            <ul class="fl">
              <li>Continuously measured data quality</li>
              <li>Structured annotation pipelines</li>
              <li>Failure-driven retraining</li>
              <li>Rollback as operational control</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="card">
            <h3>Secure Multi-Tenant Delivery</h3>
            <ul class="fl">
              <li>Strict tenant isolation</li>
              <li>Granular access control</li>
              <li>Lifecycle & retention management</li>
              <li>Audit-friendly access patterns</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══ Research ═══ -->
    <section id="research">
      <div class="sh"><div class="sh__bar"></div><span class="sh__text">Research & Production</span></div>

      <p>
        My peer-reviewed work addresses questions that recur in production:
      </p>
      <ul class="fl" style="margin-top: 1rem; margin-bottom: 1.75rem;">
        <li>How spatial measurements behave under noise and scale</li>
        <li>How resolution and alignment affect downstream inference</li>
        <li>How to reason about uncertainty in derived spatial products</li>
      </ul>
      <p>
        I have authored and co-authored publications in journals and conferences,
        contributing methods and frameworks now embedded in production pipelines.
      </p>
      <div class="links" style="margin-top: 2rem;">
        <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=TcDAyj0AAAAJ&hl=en"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Scholar</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══ Writing ═══ -->
    <section>
      <div class="sh"><div class="sh__bar"></div><span class="sh__text">Writing</span></div>
      <p>
        Technical notes on production AI systems, geospatial data failure modes,
        and system-level decision-making under constraints. What holds, what fails,
        and how to design systems that remain reliable as they evolve.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- ═══ Contact ═══ -->
    <section id="contact">
      <div class="sh"><div class="sh__bar"></div><span class="sh__text">Contact</span></div>
      <ul class="contact">
        <li><a href="mailto:nan.shang@droneinstitute.ai">nan.shang@droneinstitute.ai</a></li>
        <li><a href="mailto:sn1514826@gmail.com">sn1514826@gmail.com</a></li>
      </ul>
      <div class="links">
        <a href="https://github.com/leibowivz" target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub</a>
        <a href="https://scholar.google.com/citations?user=TcDAyj0AAAAJ&hl=en"
           target="_blank" rel="noopener">Google Scholar</a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <footer class="footer">
      <div class="footer__inner">
        <div class="footer__left">
          <div class="footer__logo">NS</div>
          <span class="footer__copy">Nan Shang, Ph.D.</span>
        </div>
        <span class="footer__copy">Chief Scientist & Founding Engineer</span>
      </div>
    </footer>
  </main>
</Base>
